From 7529196a008efa6aa31d2a3cae437389d3c9b7ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bogdan Lapadat <lapadat.bogdanv@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 23:16:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] qwen35 hybrid: split stage as an LRU expert cache, batch
 windows in the split, prompt lookup decoding, opt-in kernel and wait variants

STRATA_Q36_SPLIT_CACHE_MB=<MB>: the split stage keeps that many MB of streamed experts in VRAM
(least recently used out); an expert of the layer already there runs on the GPU with no copy.
The stage and cache are taken from the expert slots budget, not from the reserve.
The split now also takes decode batch windows and verify windows of up to 8 rows, and the
auto share is balanced after every step or window.
STRATA_Q36_LOOKUP=1 (STRATA_Q36_LOOKUP_K, STRATA_Q36_LOOKUP_N): greedy prompt lookup decoding,
drafts from the longest earlier match of the text tail, verified in one window; pauses after
low acceptance.
STRATA_Q36_MOE_OUT_4K=1: k_moe_out_small (fused next-layer q8_1) for n_embd up to 4096.
STRATA_Q36_SPIN_PAUSE=1, STRATA_Q36_BLOCKING_SYNC=1: router wait variants (measured slower).
STRATA_Q36_MISSLOG=<file>: per decode token and layer, the experts the CPU side gets.
